      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:ff7fe951bf9c7cd5",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a shower of rain, then the Telugu for to get soaked."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: అల్పపీడనం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అల్పపీడనం — alpapīḍanaṁ — \"a low-pressure area\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సముద్రంలో అల్పపీడనం ఏర్పడింది. samudraṁlō alpapīḍanaṁ ērpaḍindi. A low-pressure area has formed over the sea."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The weather news says it every monsoon: అల్ప, low, + పీడనం, pressure. A storm often follows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అల్పపీడనం (alpapīḍanaṁ) is a modern weather word built from two Sanskrit words: alpa, \"small, little\", and pīḍana, \"pressing, squeezing\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
